{
  "configuration_id": "config_018",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_016 (multimodal, singleprofile, pca_n2000, resnet50, concat) achieved 0.5266 acc, a clear ~4.2% gain over the RNA-only baseline config_001 (0.4849 acc), confirming the image modality is valuable. However, all completed experiments use singleprofile; we have zero evidence on whether multiprofile aggregation adds further value in the multimodal setting. Question tested: config_018 keeps the same RNA encoder (pca_n2000), image encoder (resnet50), and fusion (concat) as config_016 but switches to multiprofile with avgpool aggregation, isolating the effect of multi-profile representation. Why this is the best next experiment: It is the most natural and controlled extension of the current best result, tests a major architectural axis (single vs. multi profile) that gates many downstream decisions (aggregation method, encoder choices), and its outcome will efficiently prune or validate a large subtree of the remaining 49 configurations under a limited budget."
}

